WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.200 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  it's been 31 years since Mario hopped  onto arcade screens in Donkey Kong and  everyone's favorite portly plumber shows  no signs of slowing down his latest  adventure super mario odyssey brings him  to the Nintendo switch where once again  Princess Peach has been kidnapped by  Bowser and little ole Mario needs to  save the day  Nintendo has put in so little gameplay  mechanisms that help you on your quest  to get power moons both obvious ones and  hidden ones some of these systems are  explained in game but they may be easy  to miss while others are left a bit  vague we've put together a collection of  tips that will give you a little leg up  and get you skipping on your way to  rescuing Peach when you first get the  game spend some time jumping around  Mario's basic jump is perfect for  crossing small gaps and pouncing on  enemies but he has a wide range of tools  that are absolutely essential for games  trickier platforming moments you'll need  to have mastery of all these abilities  to find most of the moons Mario's jumps  can be modified by jumping repeatedly  using specific timing but a stomping  before you jump or leaping by crouching  before you jump these moves along with  most of his others are easy to pull off  once you're comfortable with them but  you'll want to practice so executing  them is second nature  capi the sentient hat accompanying Mario  in Odyssey is primarily used for taking  control of enemies or objects but you  can also use them to extend jumps we  suggest learning their hat throw and  leap combo as it's undoubtedly one of  the most useful moves in the game jump  in the air and throw capi then keep the  button held down to have Cappy hover a  moment while the Hat is spinning hit  crouch and jump and you'll leap forward  and launch back into the air this can be  repeat the second time to gain even more  ground thankfully mario odyssey features  an action guide where all the advanced  moves are available for you to read  about on top of that cappy will remind  you about things you can do when you're  traveling between worlds pick up coins  it can be tempting to skip a few coins  in the distance when you're running  around but coins have more value than  ever before in Odyssey instead of using  a traditional life system where each  theft counts down to a game over screen  all you see Nixon  from Mario's deep pockets there's no  punishment for dining with zero coins  but it does mean that you'll have less  to spend on goodies coins are also used  to buy things from various shops  scattered around all of these worlds  each shop usually has a top up of hearts  on offer as well as a moon that was  looking to get every single moon in the  game we'll want to be especially  diligent about grabbing coins as more  moons become available to purchase from  shops later in the game of course coins  are also used to purchase new outfits  for Mario and you have to purchase the  hat and jumpsuit portions separately and  trust us you'll want all of them they  don't change the way Mario plays by  adding abilities but it's pretty darn  cool to see him dressed up as a cowboy  or a racecar driver to fly to a new  location your ship needs a certain  amount of moose to power it and the game  denotes the recommended amount on screen  the simplest way to find easy to just  play through each world and keep your  eyes peeled for them as many are visible  along the main path however if you're  going for the full moon completion  you'll need to explore as there's quite  a few hidden away behind puzzles  thankfully when you complete an area by  being a boss hint toad will appear near  the Odyssey as the name implies hint  told will mark the location of a moon on  your map for 50 coins which is very  useful you might think that's a bit of a  cheat but it's still quite tricky to get  these moons as indicators are just a  vague hint of where they are for those  that need a little extra guidance they  stalker to a loose lip wide jaw parity  that hangs around the main hub of each  area chat to talk or to and it will tell  you the name of the Moon which usually  provides some further insight into where  they are or what you need to do to grab  them bear in mind that there's a limit  to how many times you can use hint toad  and torpor to moon's make a little  twinkling sound when you're close by  on your travels around the world make  sure to keep your ears open as well as  your eyes pealed it can be easy to set  your sight on a moon on the main path  and focus on it but you'll often find  that there are extra months tucked away  behind secret walls or place just out of  view another way to find hidden moons or  coins is through control of vibrations  this one is much trickier as running  around usually also makes the controller  vibrate just a little bit  however the feedback should be stronger  when you're near a secret I am a lo of  goodies hidden underground usually have  a shaft of colorful light to draw your  attention to them but this isn't always  the case so pay attention to those  vibrations a more delightful way of  finding hidden items is to let the  adorable little Nintendogs sniff them  out for you you'll find him very early  in the game chilling out in a shop in  the desert world but after you complete  that world he'll venture out when you  see him he'll excitedly bark at you and  run off into the distance give chase and  he'll lead you to something good in turn  dog will appear in other locations  during your journey so keep an eye out  for him and once he's found something  for you why not show your appreciation  and play frisbee with him Chuck Cappy at  the puppy from a distance and he'll grab  it in his mouth it's wonderful scattered  around each of oddities words are little  puzzle rooms they're accessed by finding  doors with little hats on them or by  jumping down the iconic green pipes each  of these rooms will test your mastery of  platforming or ask you to possess an  enemy using Kathy and then use their  unique abilities to solve a puzzle or  reach areas inaccessible to Mario in his  tiny human form the extra secret with  these rooms is they usually have more  than one moon hiding within them this  isn't the case a hundred percent of the  time but it pays to go into each one  with the mindset that there's more than  meets the eye in there be extra vigilant  when running through them and take the  time to stop frequently and spin the  camera around a bit you'll often find a  moon is only visible if you're looking  at it from a specific angle if that  wasn't enough keep your eyes out for  little Rockets by getting over to these  and then throwing capping on them you  can blast off into the clouds and into  more secret areas where naturally even  more moons await when you're flowing  over the planet in Odyssey you can hit  the Y button to bring up stats on each  world this menu has essential  information on all the  available in each location making it  easy to see what you have and what  remains it's a simple touch that makes  getting 100% completion just a little  more manageable  another character in Super Mario odyssey  that's quite useful is uncle amiibo the  little Roomba like device hovering  around near the ship if you're a  collector of Nintendo's amiibo figures  they'll come in very handy as they can  be used to locate stray moons tap your  amiibo on the NFC reader and uncle  amiibo will send it out on a hunt it  takes around five minutes  but once that time is up he'll let you  know where you can find a new moon  there's a limit on how many times you  can use uncle I'm able to find moons so  it's better to use him when you're  really struggling amiibo are also useful  for a little coin injection if you touch  a figure while just out in the world you  can get some coins to add to your purse  this is useful when you're a little  short on funds and want to purchase an  item from the shop for maximum  efficiency get uncle amiibo to send out  three amiibos to hunt for moons then go  out and try and grab some yourself when  you get back there'll be a few more for  you to venture out for this assumes of  course that you have three amiibo if you  don't you can just use the same amiibo  over and over again there you have it  five tips for all you would be plumbers  about to embark on an odyssey Super  Mario Odyssey is a big game and we'll be  digging into a deeper over the coming  days in the meantime you can check out  our video review or head to GameSpot  they'll come to read our full written  review  [Music]

